# 7.cicd-slowtest-report

make the cicd slow-test report actually report, so the next diagnosis starts from data.

.guard = a cicd run surfaces a RANKED per-file duration table, and the top row is
  legible as the wall-clock floor.

.hardwon = 🔴 THE REPORT WAS DEAD, SILENTLY, ON EVERY RUN. it filtered
  `select(.perfStats.runtime != null)`. jest 30 emits NO perfStats key at all — its
  --json testResults carry only assertionResults, endTime, message, name, startTime,
  status, summary. so the filter matched zero rows and the step printed no output.
  a dead instrument reads exactly like a fast suite. this is why the longest pole in
  the suite went unseen.

.hardwon = the same absent key silently broke MY instrument too — every per-file cost
  read 0.0s for hours and I skimmed past it, because 0.0s next to a real total looks
  like a rounding artifact rather than a dead read. ⇒ when a metric reads zero, prove
  it is zero before you accept it.

.hardwon = annotations alone cannot be RANKED. a diagnosis needs the order, so the fix
  writes a sorted table to GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY beside the per-file annotations.

.hardwon = re-derive a report from the RAW payload, never from a summary saved at run
  time. once `report` re-read the raw jest json, one parse fix made every past run
  re-readable — instead of one re-run per bug, at 12 minutes each.
